{
  "case_id": "2006-06-157",
  "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Solicitor General Paul D. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In Flast against Cohen, this Court recognized narrow circumstances in which a taxpayer could satisfy the requirements of Article III in challenging a congressional exercise of its spending and taxing authority. This court in doing so rejected the suggestion of Justice Douglas that it allow all taxpayers to sue in all manner of claims, as well as the slightly more modest suggestion of Justices Stewart and Fortas that the Court allow taxpayer standing for all establishment clause challenges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument this morning in case 06-157, Hein versus Freedom From Religion Foundation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: If I understand your position correctly, if Congress enacts a program that favors religion over non-religion, which is supposedly what the establishment clause prohibits, that's bad; but if Congress enacts a perfectly valid general program and the President implements it in a fashion that favors religion over non-religion, that's okay, insofar as the ability of anybody to challenge it is concerned. Is that an accurate description?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I had the same question as Justice Ginsburg, and I think was also suggested by Justice Scalia's question. Suppose that Congress passed a statute that said we hereby appropriate a million dollars to the President to use to call religious conferences, and then it spelled out these conferences. Is there standing there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: And why should that make any difference if the entire theory behind it is sort of a Madisonian theory, if not threepence from the pocket for a religious purpose? If you start with the Madisonian view, there should be no distinction of the two cases that Justice Scalia puts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: General Clement, are you -- are arguing that these lines that you're drawing make a lot of sense in an abstract sense? Or are you just arguing that this is the best that can be done that this is the best that can be done within the body of precedent that the Court has handed down in this area?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Getting upset is a constitutionally adequate reason to bring a lawsuit? If people get upset about spending money for purposes that the Federal Government is not allowed to spend money for because of States' rights, that also would justify Article III standing, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ANDREW J. PINCUS, ESQ. ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's argument here is that Flast needs major surgery and, as the discussion I think in the first part of the argument shows, it's proposing two very substantial limitations that bear no relation to the relevant establishment clause principles, the history of the clause, or the history of this Court's decisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew J. Pincus",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: Well, I don't -- I don't think that lawsuit could be brought, Mr. Chief Justice, and let me explain why. We think that the limitations that are in this Court's opinions require the taxpayer to identify a discrete and identifiable non-incidental expenditure. In other words, it's not just any --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew J. Pincus",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: The money has to be central to the violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Pincus",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: But their claim was that the spending of this entire grant is unconstitutional because of the way the money is going to be used by the grantees. It wasn't that $1.98 of the is unconstitutional and the other million dollars is okay. It was that because of the way the grantee was using the money, the entire grant is unconstitutional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Pincus, may I ask you this question? Do you think your theory is consistent with Valley Forge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think the distinction between taxing, between taxing and spending and the property clause, makes any sense? Do you think James Madison would not be upset if the Commonwealth of Virginia transferred 10,000 acres to the Anglican Church? That would be okay, but the threepence in taxation would not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PINCUS",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think that the Court decided that it made a difference, and I think in terms of cabining, in terms of the worry that perhaps Flast is going to be overbroad and the need to have Congress involved, which I think is key -- there was no congressional involvement at all in designating those properties and there is in the appropriations context, and I think that's a key difference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "GENERAL CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, I think it's important to emphasize that if this Court recognizes that there is not taxpayer standing, that does not mean that there won't be lawsuits, that there won't be directly injured plaintiffs that can bring claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2006-06-157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, general. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
